## Round 2: judge results, ham prompt for try 5, and the try 5 call

Commit of the round 2 judge records: `29ab198a`
(`measure(storytime_l2_card_line_retry): family try 4 passes, ham try 4 fails`).
Commit of the try 5 prompt: `a910c930` (`feat(storytime_l2_card_line_retry): ham line prompt for
try 5`).

### Judge results of round 1

- Family try 4: `pass`, result file `judge-cards-retry-family-t4.json`. The row is delivered at
  try 4 and Task 5 is `[x]`.
- Ham try 4: `fail`, defect class `wrong-or-missing-prop`, result file
  `judge-cards-retry-ham-t4.json`. The second judge on the same file also fails, result file
  `judge-cards-retry-ham-t4-second.json`. The fail stands.
- Orchestrator decision 2026-11-07: ham try 5 is the last ham try.

### Ham try 5 prompt

The `linePrompt` is the exact text of the orchestrator brief of 2026-11-07: a wide, lopsided oval
slice with the fat rim along the top edge only, and no round disc, ring, or scallop. `colorPrompt`,
`mustShow`, `goal`, `references`, and every other field are byte equal. Card spec test: 10 tests
pass, exit 0. Commit `a910c930`.

### Ham try 5 call

- First call: `network error: UND_ERR_CONNECT_TIMEOUT`, cost 0 USD, output `none`, time
  `2026-11-07T03:00:44.344Z`. A zero-cost failure is not a try, so the maker repeated the call
  once, as the spec allows.
- Repeat: `ok 1600x1600 cost 0.01`, output `l2-w04-card-ham-m1-line-5.png`, note `redo 5`, time
  `2026-11-07T03:01:31.651Z`, running total 0.9800 USD.
- Width: `l2-w04-card-ham-m1-line-print-5.png` at 1500 x 1500 measures 36 px (gate 12 px),
  coverage 14.60%, SHA-256
  `0d874ba2a39d3760f20f26ca8d0c7653b632404e5667f7b9ee21e5ea5b78e93c`. Record:
  `line-widths-r2.txt`.
- `costs.tsv` now holds 99 rows and 0.9800 USD. The track spend is 0.03 USD.
- The ham allowance is full: the two line tries since the start time are `-line-4` and `-line-5`,
  and the ham limit is 2. No further ham call is allowed.

### Blocked judge batch

- Command: `node scripts/storytime-judge-batch.mjs --cards --ids l2-w04-card-ham --kind line
  --try 5 --out cards-retry-ham-t5`.
- Result: exit 1, `error: the line try 5 of l2-w04-card-ham has no picture file (the call
  failed).` Log: `judge-batch-retry-r2.log`. No batch file exists.
- Cause: `restartTries` of the builder reads every cost row of the id and kind in time order. The
  zero-cost failure row is the 5th such row, and its output column is `none`. The builder counts
  it as try 5 and refuses it. The picture file is the 6th row (`-line-5.png`).
- The builder is a frozen file (FR-12). The maker does not change it. This is a decision for the
  orchestrator.

### Question for the orchestrator

The batch builder counts the zero-cost failure row as try 5. The three options:

- (A) Build the batch with `--try 6`. The judge copy becomes `l2-w04-card-ham-line-t6.png` while
  the Muse file is `-line-5.png`. The judge sees the right picture, but the copy name and the
  result file say try 6.
- (B) Authorize a one-line change in `scripts/storytime-judge-batch.mjs`: skip a row whose output
  is `none` in `restartTries`. Then `--try 5` builds the batch with the copy
  `l2-w04-card-ham-line-t5.png`. This matches the spec rule that a zero-cost failure is not a try,
  but it changes a frozen file (FR-12) and needs your word.
- (C) Accept the ham row as failed at try 5 with no judge. That breaks the spec rule that every
  ham try goes to the judge.

Default if no answer: (B) only with your authorization; otherwise (A) with the t6 copy note in the
record.

### Resolution: option (A)

Orchestrator answer 2026-11-07: option (A). The builder did not change.

- The cost rows of `l2-w04-card-ham` with kind `line` since the card start time, in time order:
  1. `l2-w04-card-ham-m1-line.png`, 2. `-line-2.png`, 3. `-line-3.png`, 4. `-line-4.png`,
  5. `null` (the network failure), 6. `l2-w04-card-ham-m1-line-5.png`. Position 6 holds the try 5
  picture.
- Command: `node scripts/storytime-judge-batch.mjs --cards --ids l2-w04-card-ham --kind line
  --try 6 --out cards-retry-ham-t5`, exit 0.
- Batch: `docs/storytime/l2-unit1/judge/prod/cards-retry-ham-t5.json`. Judge copy:
  `out/storytime-review/judge/prod/l2-w04-card-ham-line-t6.png` at 360 x 360.
- Source check: the judge copy is byte equal to a 360 px copy of
  `l2-w04-card-ham-m1-line-5.png` (SHA-256
  `d742e3134ff77d14958494855cc38de2631c18e3d7b91096059f9db2bb040695`). A 360 px copy of the
  print file has a different SHA-256, because the print file is the 1500 px crop.
- The orchestrator note is in `judge-batch-retry-r2.log`: the zero-cost network failure row holds
  builder position 5, so `--try 6` selects the try 5 picture; the judge copy is named
  `line-t6.png`; the frozen builder did not change.

